<header class="start-masthead"><p class="eyebrow">Lab runtime · proposed documentation</p><h1>Provision a branch and review its authority</h1><p>Separate environment selection, store creation, key custody and approval.</p><p class="source-note">Draft prepared on 2026-10-14. Integration and final T21 qualification remain pending.</p></header>

<section id="runtime-provision-choose-the-kind-of-provisioning" aria-labelledby="runtime-provision-choose-the-kind-of-provisioning-title"><h2 id="runtime-provision-choose-the-kind-of-provisioning-title">Choose the kind of provisioning</h2>

<p>Local v1 init creates a new operational branch. Candidate provisioning constructs a separately scoped branch from pinned runtime/configuration/baseline/HEAD. Composite operator preparation additionally selects three independent branch workspaces, policies and authentication proofs. These actions are not interchangeable.</p>

<p>Read <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-provisioning/candidates/v1/provision.py">CandidateScope and CandidateBranch</a> for controlled branch construction, <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-bootstrap/candidates/v1/bootstrap.py">bootstrap composition</a> for seed packaging, and <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-runtime/ADMISSION.md">v1 admission</a> for its local scope. A package, key, store and admitted implementation each answer a different question.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-provision-check-the-environment-before-the-branch" aria-labelledby="runtime-provision-check-the-environment-before-the-branch-title"><h2 id="runtime-provision-check-the-environment-before-the-branch-title">Check the environment before the branch</h2>

<p>Select the exact executable, parser, profile, dependency closure and supported filesystem assumptions. T07&#x27;s <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T07/revision-0002/dependency-selection-0002.json">1010-file selected dependency declaration</a> identifies installation0004; its existence is not a new-install witness or a blanket compatibility result for every package.</p>

<p>Confirm the source cut and current byte checks before selecting a new store. A historical profile may be useful for inspection while lacking current records. Installing Python/native dependencies does not initialize a branch, provision authority or activate a service. The <a href="runtime-cli.html">CLI/environment reference</a> keeps those interfaces separate.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-provision-keep-credential-custody-explicit" aria-labelledby="runtime-provision-keep-credential-custody-explicit-title"><h2 id="runtime-provision-keep-credential-custody-explicit-title">Keep credential custody explicit</h2>

<p>A local approver key remains outside Git and outside public artifacts. A reader policy selects a bounded Principal, source, scope, operations, budgets, expiry and nonce channel. Private signing bytes, credential paths with real secrets and live private policy bodies do not belong in task text, replies, exports or tutorial logs.</p>

<p>For the composite candidate, Base, Action and Governance need independent current branch selectors and three proofs. The <a href="research/sources/product/lab/release-candidates/v1/interface/composite-operator-v1-completion-0001/revision-0003/README.md">operator contract</a> explicitly selects the outer policy custody root separately from Base&#x27;s actual nested Vault and its original workspace/workspace.json. Copying an outer manifest cannot stand in for the real Vault.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-provision-review-before-authorizing" aria-labelledby="runtime-provision-review-before-authorizing-title"><h2 id="runtime-provision-review-before-authorizing-title">Review before authorizing</h2>

<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">What it establishes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Environment/source inspection</td><td>The selected inputs are available and match declared bytes</td></tr><tr><td>Branch initialization</td><td>A new scoped store/configuration exists</td></tr><tr><td>Candidate review</td><td>Consequences, contracts, source cut and unresolved obligations are visible</td></tr><tr><td>Exact signed authorization</td><td>This local approver approved these bytes within this boundary</td></tr><tr><td>Application and cold replay</td><td>The observed scoped effect and its committed chain</td></tr><tr><td>Repository admission or service activation</td><td>Separate governing and operational evidence</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p>Review failures stay attached to their exact input version. A technical provisioning receipt cannot become Action/Governance or genuine owner authority merely by being passed to another component.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-provision-when-provisioning-refuses" aria-labelledby="runtime-provision-when-provisioning-refuses-title"><h2 id="runtime-provision-when-provisioning-refuses-title">When provisioning refuses</h2>

<p>An existing path, changed baseline/HEAD, unsafe root, missing public key, expired/revoked policy or unknown execution origin should refuse. Preserve the actual error and owned partial state. Choose a separately authorized new branch or correct a new candidate version; do not silently overwrite, restore old Session RAM or extend a historical period.</p>

<p>Fresh setup and full three-branch operation remain pending for the changed API17 composition. Follow <a href="runtime-status.html">status</a> and <a href="runtime-recovery.html">recovery</a> before interpreting a refusal as a reason to rerun.</p>

</section>

